WEBVTT

01:41.000 --> 01:41.960
ORGANISM LIMITS

01:41.960 --> 01:43.750
ORGANISM LIMITS
Well, this is a surprise.

01:43.750 --> 01:43.830
ORGANISM LIMITS

01:43.830 --> 01:44.750
ORGANISM LIMITS
I never expected Zombieman to be a
test subject from the House of Evolution.

01:44.750 --> 01:47.920
I never expected Zombieman to be a
test subject from the House of Evolution.

01:48.590 --> 01:52.340
I have many memories of Sample No. 66.

01:52.720 --> 01:54.800
You were an excellent specimen
and my only success

01:54.800 --> 01:56.720
in my immortality experiments.

01:56.850 --> 01:59.770
But then, you destroyed the lab
and disappeared.

02:00.100 --> 02:02.060
That was over ten years ago.

02:02.480 --> 02:04.440
And now, you've become a hero.

02:04.770 --> 02:07.230
You actually managed to change yourself.

02:08.900 --> 02:12.030
So you're going to kill me?
That's fine too.

02:12.110 --> 02:14.070
Why did the House of Evolution
disappear?

02:14.360 --> 02:17.280
You can rebuild it as many times
as you want, as long as you're alive.

02:17.740 --> 02:19.540
Answer me, Dr. Genus!

02:20.040 --> 02:22.330
My research was a failure.

02:22.330 --> 02:26.750
I witnessed a power that
far surpassed artificial evolution.

02:27.210 --> 02:29.460
He removed his limiter.

02:29.800 --> 02:30.920
Limiter?

02:30.960 --> 02:32.880
No matter how much
an organism strives

02:32.880 --> 02:35.930
there are limits to its growth.

02:36.970 --> 02:40.140
An overabundance of strength is
a burden to its bearer

02:40.310 --> 02:42.060
and can cause malfunctions.

02:42.270 --> 02:45.440
Or they may become a monster who
has lost all humanity

02:45.440 --> 02:47.150
and rage out of control.

02:47.770 --> 02:49.520
For that reason

02:49.520 --> 02:52.900
God has designed each creature
to grow within parameters

02:52.940 --> 02:56.070
that allow for survival and
the preservation of reason.

03:32.980 --> 03:34.990
And that is what a limiter is.

03:35.650 --> 03:37.450
But he was different.

03:37.570 --> 03:40.160
By pushing himself
beyond his boundaries

03:40.160 --> 03:43.290
he removed his limiter and
obtained unfathomable strength.

03:43.410 --> 03:48.420
Is strength without a limiter
something one can gain without any cost?

03:48.670 --> 03:51.210
Of course not, he paid a price.

03:51.960 --> 03:54.550
In exchange for his strength,
he went bald.

03:54.550 --> 03:57.680
He also suffers from the loneliness
that comes with such overwhelming power.

03:57.680 --> 04:01.300
After defeating the strongest warrior
in my lab’s history with a single punch

04:01.300 --> 04:04.350
the look on his face said it all.

04:04.640 --> 04:05.730
Ridiculous.

04:05.770 --> 04:08.390
Sounds like
the only malfunction caused

04:08.390 --> 04:10.400
by your bizarre research
was in your own head.

04:10.900 --> 04:15.610
I have seen many monsters who've
ignored the limits of their abilities.

04:16.740 --> 04:18.820
Most likely this is far beyond...

04:18.910 --> 04:21.240
...what you’re imagining.

04:21.530 --> 04:23.410
The triggers for becoming a monster vary.

04:23.410 --> 04:24.740
A spiraling obsession or

04:24.740 --> 04:27.040
an inferiority complex leading to
a desire to transform

04:27.040 --> 04:30.080
or an explosion of pent-up frustration.

04:30.080 --> 04:31.630
The causes may vary

04:31.630 --> 04:33.750
but in every case their cells
suffer abnormalities

04:33.750 --> 04:35.760
and they became mutated creatures.

04:36.260 --> 04:38.220
Others, like those born
from my research

04:38.220 --> 04:41.050
were deliberately created
through scientific means.

04:41.340 --> 04:44.470
Many non-human creatures
mutate into monstrous forms

04:44.470 --> 04:47.140
due to environmental pollution
or other factors.

04:47.640 --> 04:50.100
But that is simply
becoming another species.

04:50.100 --> 04:52.230
It is not the same as
breaking the limiter.

04:52.480 --> 04:54.690
The Clan of the Seafolk
who attacked City J

04:54.690 --> 04:56.400
and the aliens
that appeared in City A

04:56.400 --> 04:58.360
can be broadly classified as monsters.

04:58.860 --> 05:01.110
But they were always creatures
like that from the start

05:01.110 --> 05:04.080
and natural enemies of mankind
with an intelligence of their own.

05:04.450 --> 05:09.710
Heroes possess the great power
to confront and fight against them.

05:09.750 --> 05:12.630
Those heroes are born with
the potential to become strong

05:12.670 --> 05:15.920
and they cultivated it
through effort and talent.

05:16.090 --> 05:17.960
Some have undergone
cybernetic enhancements

05:17.960 --> 05:21.840
or have acquired special abilities
through human experimentation, like you.

05:22.010 --> 05:25.010
Some are born as
extraordinary geniuses like me

05:25.010 --> 05:26.680
or gifted with unique abilities.

05:27.100 --> 05:29.390
But he was different.

05:29.640 --> 05:33.520
Born ordinary, lived an ordinary life,
and possessed no special talent.

05:33.520 --> 05:35.110
He was just a regular person.

05:35.110 --> 05:37.980
But through sheer effort alone
he forced open the door to his limits

05:37.980 --> 05:39.820
and shattered his limiter.

05:40.280 --> 05:42.530
The strength of someone
who has removed their limiter

05:42.530 --> 05:45.160
and undergone self-evolution
is truly remarkable...

05:45.910 --> 05:48.450
Just thinking about it
now makes me laugh

05:48.450 --> 05:51.040
at how absurd my own ambitions were.

05:51.580 --> 05:54.250
One day, you may have
a chance to meet him too.

05:54.580 --> 05:57.000
Apparently, he's also a hero.

05:57.710 --> 05:59.340
Do you have any more questions?

05:59.550 --> 06:01.630
So why takoyaki?

06:02.050 --> 06:04.180
While researching human regeneration

06:04.220 --> 06:07.260
I found a way to endlessly
regenerate octopus legs.

06:07.430 --> 06:08.260
I see.

06:14.060 --> 06:15.230
<i>I can beat these guys.</i>

06:15.480 --> 06:18.320
<i>They're nothing compared</i>
<i>to the old geezer.</i>

06:18.650 --> 06:21.190
I can't believe a human
could go this far.

06:21.440 --> 06:25.280
It's two against one.
You must be pretty strong.

06:26.740 --> 06:30.540
I was gonna toy
with you a bit, but forget it.

06:30.580 --> 06:31.620
Let's finish this...

06:31.830 --> 06:33.410
The real fight starts now.

06:33.960 --> 06:36.000
I've figured out all your moves.

06:39.880 --> 06:41.510
You'll never hit me again.

06:42.880 --> 06:43.760
Old dude...

06:44.090 --> 06:44.930
Hm?

06:45.010 --> 06:46.390
- Oh.
- Huh?

06:49.850 --> 06:53.100
Old dude... Sorry...

06:53.560 --> 06:56.190
Hedro-Jellyfish, what brings you here?

06:56.480 --> 06:59.900
I've got a personal grudge
with that guy.

07:00.230 --> 07:01.360
<i>That bastard...</i>

07:02.400 --> 07:04.610
Hey! That damn brat's got
nothing to do with this!

07:17.790 --> 07:18.670
Oh my.

07:19.000 --> 07:19.840
Hey!

07:20.290 --> 07:22.550
Weren't the orders not to kill him?

07:22.630 --> 07:25.680
You should've stopped me sooner,
Insect God.

07:26.090 --> 07:30.100
Too late now, he's dead.

07:30.890 --> 07:35.100
Phew... Come on,
let's all get out of here.

07:42.820 --> 07:44.240
BLEEP BLEEP

07:44.320 --> 07:46.150
WHACK
BLIP BLOP

07:46.240 --> 07:47.990
<i>Why did he want to</i>
<i>watch me play a game?</i>

07:47.990 --> 07:49.160
<i>What's he up to?</i>

07:49.620 --> 07:51.490
BA-DA-DA-DAAA!
So I cleared the game.

07:51.490 --> 07:51.620
BA-DA-DA-DAAA!

07:51.620 --> 07:52.620
BA-DA-DA-DAAA!
So? You happy now?

07:52.620 --> 07:53.580
So? You happy now?

07:53.870 --> 07:55.250
Is it over already?

07:55.540 --> 07:57.540
I didn't understand it at all.

07:58.120 --> 08:01.290
<i>So it's still too soon for me to</i>
<i>join the simulated battles</i>

08:01.340 --> 08:04.010
<i>that Master Saitama and King</i>
<i>usually play.</i>

08:04.300 --> 08:05.840
<i>I need to level up more.</i>

08:06.050 --> 08:07.470
<i>So many things I need to work on.</i>

08:07.760 --> 08:10.090
It's getting late.

08:10.300 --> 08:13.680
You won't find Garou
just by searching blindly.

08:13.680 --> 08:16.600
He's most likely holed up with
the monsters at their hideout.

08:16.730 --> 08:18.770
Master's resolve seemed unshakable.

08:18.900 --> 08:21.770
Until he discovers and destroys
the Monster Association's base

08:21.770 --> 08:23.110
he might not return.

08:23.440 --> 08:26.740
Saitama is strong
but with that personality

08:26.740 --> 08:28.150
I'm a little worried.

08:28.240 --> 08:30.620
If he were to fall into
the monsters' trap by chance...

08:34.740 --> 08:35.950
I'm home!

08:36.290 --> 08:37.330
It's Master!

08:37.370 --> 08:38.750
He came back
like it was nothing.

08:38.870 --> 08:40.790
Were you successful?

08:41.080 --> 08:42.630
Geez...

08:42.920 --> 08:43.960
Phew...

08:45.090 --> 08:46.960
Man, that was a disaster...

08:47.470 --> 08:49.050
What a mess I got into.

08:49.260 --> 08:50.130
- What?!
- What?!

08:50.130 --> 08:52.800
Don't tell me you really
found Garou?

08:53.140 --> 08:55.850
What? You guys are still here?

08:56.310 --> 08:57.640
It's too cramped in here.

08:57.770 --> 09:00.690
Master! There is blood on you.
Is it from the Hero Hunter?

09:00.810 --> 09:02.690
No, I ran into a monster
on my way home.

09:02.690 --> 09:04.320
Was it from
the Monster Association?

09:04.480 --> 09:07.490
No, there are always
monsters around here.

09:07.820 --> 09:09.070
Who knows why?

09:09.780 --> 09:12.200
Anyway, that's not the problem at all.

09:12.450 --> 09:15.830
What happened that
was so disastrous?

09:16.160 --> 09:17.870
You were all fired up when you left.

09:18.080 --> 09:19.620
Who did what to you?

09:21.710 --> 09:22.880
The thing is...

09:24.170 --> 09:25.960
I dropped my wallet somewhere.

09:26.550 --> 09:28.550
It had about 6,000 yen inside.

09:29.170 --> 09:33.390
That's all? I thought
you had a run in with Garou.

09:33.470 --> 09:35.930
Oh no!
Now that you mention it.

09:35.930 --> 09:37.140
Yeah, what happened?

09:37.890 --> 09:40.180
Th-That dine-and-dasher!

09:40.310 --> 09:41.890
You know who it is?

09:42.350 --> 09:44.230
When I was chasing him...

09:44.940 --> 09:48.530
The napa cabbage I bought!
I left it in a family restaurant!

09:48.780 --> 09:50.820
Oh no. I'll go recover it.

09:50.860 --> 09:53.490
No, Genos.
You cannot with those injuries.

09:53.570 --> 09:55.280
All this over napa cabbage?

09:56.330 --> 09:57.700
Sounds like you're all having fun.

09:58.120 --> 10:02.210
You're back again, Hellish Blizzard?
What do you want this time?

10:02.250 --> 10:04.540
Saitama... How dare you.

10:06.670 --> 10:09.840
Is... Is that the napa cabbage?
Why does Blizzard have it?

10:10.260 --> 10:12.010
Here, you forgot this.

10:12.170 --> 10:13.800
Yay, you saved the day!

10:13.930 --> 10:16.050
I feel like having hot pot tonight.

10:16.680 --> 10:18.930
And what's a hot pot
without napa cabbage!

10:19.020 --> 10:21.980
Don't you have
anything else to say to me?

10:22.310 --> 10:24.560
Huh? Thanks for the napa cabbage.

10:25.230 --> 10:31.400
No! Apologize for sticking me
with the bill at the restaurant!

10:31.570 --> 10:34.530
Oh yeah, forgot about that.
S-Sorry.

10:34.700 --> 10:36.950
You even left in the middle
of our conversation again!

10:36.990 --> 10:39.370
Huh? Were we talking
about something?

10:39.410 --> 10:41.370
See, I knew you weren't listening!

10:41.580 --> 10:45.880
Anyway, you owe me one.
Don't you forget it!

10:46.420 --> 10:48.880
<i>She knows</i>
<i>she's not in our league.</i>

10:48.880 --> 10:50.130
<i>Why does</i>
<i>she keep coming around?</i>

10:50.880 --> 10:52.970
<i>Does she also want to</i>
<i>become Master's disciple?</i>

10:53.260 --> 10:55.590
<i>It'd be a hassle</i>
<i>if Master's workload increases.</i>

10:55.680 --> 10:57.890
<i>I must prevent that at all costs.</i>

10:59.180 --> 11:00.680
High-speed approach detected.

11:00.720 --> 11:01.640
Something is coming!

11:02.020 --> 11:02.850
<i>Damn it.</i>

11:02.850 --> 11:05.230
<i>With these injuries,</i>
<i>I won't be able to fight properly.</i>

11:05.520 --> 11:07.150
<i>Bang and his brother are injured.</i>

11:07.230 --> 11:11.230
<i>Blizzard likely wouldn't stand a chance</i>
<i>if the enemy is Demon level or above.</i>

11:11.730 --> 11:15.110
<i>Master has suffered serious psychological</i>
<i>damage from losing his wallet.</i>

11:15.240 --> 11:17.450
<i>The only one</i>
<i>who can fight right now is...</i>

11:18.240 --> 11:22.080
King! An enemy approaches,
go outside and intercept it.

11:22.330 --> 11:23.160
Huh?

11:23.290 --> 11:25.000
- We cannot allow a fight in here.
- Why not?

11:25.000 --> 11:25.830
PUSH PUSH
- We cannot allow a fight in here.
- Why not?

11:25.830 --> 11:26.710
PUSH PUSH
Just go outside!

11:26.710 --> 11:28.670
PUSH PUSH
Wait, there's no need to push.

11:28.670 --> 11:30.090
PUSH PUSH
Let's calm down.
What's going on?

11:30.090 --> 11:30.130
PUSH PUSH

11:30.130 --> 11:32.000
PUSH PUSH
Don't worry.
There's only one enemy.

11:32.000 --> 11:32.880
But why?!

11:33.460 --> 11:34.590
What's going on, Genos?

11:34.670 --> 11:37.510
A monster has come,
but I asked King to take care of it.

11:37.640 --> 11:38.470
Uh-oh...

11:39.140 --> 11:39.510
RUMBLE RUMBLE

11:39.510 --> 11:42.220
RUMBLE RUMBLE
It was right outside the front door.

11:42.220 --> 11:42.260
It was right outside the front door.

11:42.310 --> 11:42.680
HISS HISS

11:42.680 --> 11:43.680
HISS HISS
You have a visitor.

11:43.680 --> 11:43.930
HISS HISS
What the...? King!
Why would you invite it in?

11:43.930 --> 11:45.770
What the...? King!
Why would you invite it in?

11:45.770 --> 11:46.060
No, wait. Looks like you've been
badly damaged again.

11:46.060 --> 11:47.690
HISS HISS
No, wait. Looks like you've been
badly damaged again.

11:47.690 --> 11:49.400
No, wait. Looks like you've been
badly damaged again.

11:49.400 --> 11:49.810
You mustn't push yourself.

11:49.810 --> 11:51.440
HISS HISS
You mustn't push yourself.

11:51.440 --> 11:51.820
You mustn't push yourself.

11:52.190 --> 11:54.110
It's me, Genos.

11:55.240 --> 11:56.490
Dr. Kuseno!

11:56.650 --> 11:58.700
You know him?
What a relief.

11:58.780 --> 11:59.910
Why are you here?

11:59.990 --> 12:01.910
I was worried about you.

12:02.120 --> 12:06.460
Soon after I repaired you,
I received another distress signal.

12:06.500 --> 12:09.710
So I wanted to personally check in
on you and see what's going on.

12:09.750 --> 12:11.750
I'm sorry to worry you.

12:11.960 --> 12:14.000
I said I wouldn't lose again,
and yet...

12:14.090 --> 12:15.380
I'm surprised.

12:15.460 --> 12:19.220
I had improved your systems
and firepower considerably...

12:19.510 --> 12:21.140
Well, don't worry about it.

12:21.220 --> 12:24.100
Your life is more important
than winning.

12:24.390 --> 12:27.730
So what happened to the enemy
that damaged you so badly?

12:28.190 --> 12:30.310
As usual, Master Saitama defeated it...

12:30.560 --> 12:32.400
I see... So you must be...

12:33.020 --> 12:35.230
Genos's master, Saitama.

12:35.440 --> 12:36.740
I've always wanted to
meet you...

12:36.780 --> 12:38.320
Mind taking your shoes off?

12:38.400 --> 12:39.860
Oh! So sorry!

12:39.860 --> 12:40.950
ONE-PUNCH MAN
Oh! So sorry!

12:40.950 --> 12:41.950
ONE-PUNCH MAN

12:41.990 --> 12:43.990
ONE-PUNCH MAN

12:44.160 --> 12:45.410
I am Kuseno.

12:45.490 --> 12:48.040
I used to be just a humble
mechanical engineer

12:48.080 --> 12:51.130
but due to circumstances, I now support
Genos in his pursuit of justice.

12:51.130 --> 12:52.960
I'm Saitama.
Nice to meet you.

12:53.040 --> 12:54.000
I see...

12:54.090 --> 12:58.050
It warms my heart that Genos
has found such a respectable mentor.

12:58.420 --> 12:59.970
When Genos and I first met...

13:00.010 --> 13:03.010
- He came to pick you up Genos!
- ...we had no allies at all.

13:03.010 --> 13:06.470
- It's cramped in here, so let's wrap!
- We wandered through the darkness...

13:06.470 --> 13:07.980
- Later, Kuseno!
- We battled evil...

13:07.980 --> 13:10.850
Doctor, please summarize
in 20 characters or less.

13:11.060 --> 13:12.770
Oh, come on.
Don't say that.

13:12.810 --> 13:15.440
Since I knew that I would be
visiting Saitama's place

13:15.570 --> 13:17.110
I brought a little something.

13:17.150 --> 13:19.360
Is it some kind of
enhancement part for Master?

13:19.490 --> 13:20.950
Hey, I'm human, you know...

13:21.030 --> 13:24.700
The ultimate premium deluxe beef gift set.

13:24.740 --> 13:26.330
Top quality.

13:26.620 --> 13:29.080
Think of it as a token of gratitude
for taking care of Genos.

13:29.080 --> 13:31.120
Will you please accept it?

13:31.210 --> 13:33.380
Oh? Fancy meat, huh...

13:33.460 --> 13:36.130
I haven't had meat in ages...

13:36.340 --> 13:37.880
Kuseno...

13:37.880 --> 13:39.260
...I mean, Dr. Kuseno.

13:39.920 --> 13:44.140
As Genos's mentors,
I'm sure we have a lot to talk about.

13:44.510 --> 13:47.220
Please feel free to
drop by anytime you like!

13:47.310 --> 13:49.180
<i>What a sucker.</i>
<i>That was too easy.</i>

13:49.270 --> 13:52.900
<i>Now I feel silly for thinking</i>
<i>it'd be hard to recruit him.</i>

13:53.310 --> 13:55.150
Okay, let's put this
in the hot pot too.

13:55.400 --> 13:57.110
I'll go chop the vegetables.

13:57.440 --> 14:00.400
You're going to use
that premium beef for a hot pot?

14:00.490 --> 14:02.610
What a waste.

14:03.450 --> 14:05.740
Do you have any red wine here?

14:05.910 --> 14:07.370
Hm? Of course not.

14:07.450 --> 14:08.290
Oh!

14:08.540 --> 14:11.120
You're not thinking of staying
for dinner, are you?

14:11.410 --> 14:13.870
If you have no business here,
it's time to leave.

14:14.000 --> 14:16.710
Come on, King, old guys,
go on home!

14:17.420 --> 14:19.590
We had a little chat with Garou.

14:19.630 --> 14:21.760
And he failed the test.

14:22.170 --> 14:24.840
Well actually, in the heat of
the moment, we killed him.

14:25.220 --> 14:31.140
We said we just wanted to talk,
but then he suddenly attacked us!

14:31.140 --> 14:33.690
How despicable, right, Insect God?

14:34.940 --> 14:37.400
Are those worthless lies
all you've got?

14:37.940 --> 14:40.730
Tell me what really happened.

14:40.900 --> 14:44.610
He was just some half-assed guy
calling himself a monster.

14:44.740 --> 14:48.660
He could turn on us at any moment,
depending on the situation.

14:49.290 --> 14:50.330
So what?

14:50.370 --> 14:54.000
You got a problem because
we took care of him on our own?

14:54.160 --> 14:57.000
No complaints.
I'm glad you both went.

14:57.130 --> 15:00.500
You two seem pretty beaten up.
Was he strong?

15:01.550 --> 15:04.130
That lean body of his packed
way more power than I expected

15:04.130 --> 15:05.260
and took me off guard.

15:05.510 --> 15:08.220
Now I know why
you sent the two of us.

15:08.300 --> 15:10.010
So is he really dead?

15:10.010 --> 15:12.680
We didn't double-check,
but I'm pretty sure he is.

15:12.930 --> 15:15.480
It's because Insect God
was slow to stop me.

15:15.600 --> 15:18.480
You wanted to kill him from the start!

15:19.940 --> 15:20.820
<i>Old dude...</i>

15:23.070 --> 15:25.400
So, what's with the kid?

15:25.780 --> 15:28.030
He saw us, so we brought him in.

15:28.570 --> 15:29.740
What are you laughing about?

15:29.740 --> 15:31.290
Get rid of him immediately.

15:31.410 --> 15:33.450
Come on, don't get so mad.

15:33.500 --> 15:36.210
I brought him so I can take
my time tormenting him later.

15:36.290 --> 15:37.880
I gotta let off steam

15:37.880 --> 15:41.340
or I'll end up impulsively
slashing someone here again.

15:41.880 --> 15:44.050
There's no time left
for playing around.

15:44.590 --> 15:48.300
A Hero Association surveillance robot
was spotted right near our hideout.

15:48.550 --> 15:52.140
They'll pinpoint this location
in less than a day.

15:52.560 --> 15:55.020
That means the Class-S heroes
we've all been waiting for

15:55.020 --> 15:56.270
will finally be sent our way.

15:56.270 --> 15:58.480
And they're formidable opponents.

15:58.940 --> 16:01.320
Everyone, prepare for battle!

16:01.650 --> 16:03.610
Is it true it was an easy win?

16:03.650 --> 16:06.610
Yeah, Gyoro-Gyoro picks opponents
based on compatibility.

16:06.650 --> 16:08.200
Compatibility, my ass!

16:08.490 --> 16:10.820
Cowering in front of mere humans!?

16:11.120 --> 16:16.160
Strong monsters like me will
take 'em down in a head-on clash.

16:16.330 --> 16:17.620
Pathetic!

16:18.290 --> 16:21.210
If that story is true, then I should
be able to become one too...

16:21.590 --> 16:23.920
The Monster King Phoenix Man!

16:24.250 --> 16:25.800
Listen up, you guys.

16:25.970 --> 16:28.510
I want one kill from each of you.

16:28.550 --> 16:29.970
Put your life on the line!

16:30.760 --> 16:33.470
And the credit will be all mine!

16:35.890 --> 16:38.770
Didn't you hear?
No killing fellow monsters.

16:39.100 --> 16:42.770
You pseudo-monsters have
no right to defy us real monsters.

16:42.940 --> 16:44.440
Know your place!

16:44.570 --> 16:46.570
Malong Hair, you're so powerful!

16:46.570 --> 16:48.030
Are you threat level Demon?

16:48.030 --> 16:50.070
Like a tiger with wings
and chestnut long hair.

16:50.280 --> 16:53.620
Straightening my hair gave me power.
That is what created Malong Hair.

16:53.660 --> 16:57.200
Wow, so you monsterized
by doing proper hair care?

16:57.660 --> 17:02.710
Hey Nyaan, when Puri-Puri Prisoner
shows up let us take care of him.

17:02.750 --> 17:04.040
Yeah, sounds good.

17:04.210 --> 17:06.260
We're strong enough now
to get back at him.

17:06.380 --> 17:08.840
I won't be happy until
I kill that guy with my own hands.

17:09.680 --> 17:12.050
Very well.
Do as you please and go wild.

17:12.800 --> 17:16.810
The only real top-tier fighter in
the Hero Association is Flashy Flash.

17:17.310 --> 17:18.600
All the rest are just small fry.

17:18.930 --> 17:21.900
There are people with supernatural powers
and robots on their side.

17:22.690 --> 17:24.570
Robots are irrelevant.

17:24.900 --> 17:29.450
No machine could ever keep up
with a ninja's speed.

18:30.510 --> 18:31.880
What about the
supernatural powers?

18:34.340 --> 18:37.720
We'll kill them so quickly that they
won't be able to activate their powers.

18:46.940 --> 18:49.650
You're G5, right?

18:50.900 --> 18:53.780
What's that?
Did you steal that from somewhere?

18:53.860 --> 18:57.530
It's a little something I picked up
for my own interests.

18:58.080 --> 19:00.790
I plan to take it apart
and analyze it in detail.

19:00.950 --> 19:03.290
<i>Metal Knight is in pieces?!</i>

19:03.830 --> 19:05.830
It's a valuable sample.

19:06.290 --> 19:07.250
If you'll excuse me.

19:12.590 --> 19:15.840
Waganma, I brought you a friend.

19:17.430 --> 19:20.260
Who are you? I'm Tareo.

19:20.430 --> 19:22.140
Were you captured by the monsters, too?

19:22.720 --> 19:24.980
Umm...Waganma?

19:25.390 --> 19:28.560
Yeah. Hey, is it nighttime already?

19:28.860 --> 19:30.150
Y-Yeah.

19:30.690 --> 19:33.070
You got any food?

19:33.150 --> 19:37.280
I have candy. I only have one piece,
but if you want it...

19:40.780 --> 19:41.660
Anything else?

19:41.660 --> 19:43.870
S-Sorry, no.

19:44.500 --> 19:46.580
Damn, you're useless.

19:47.580 --> 19:50.710
So...what's gonna happen to us?

19:50.960 --> 19:53.420
Those monsters sure are dumb.

19:53.630 --> 19:54.460
What?

19:54.510 --> 19:56.630
I mean, of all people,
they kidnapped me!

19:56.930 --> 19:59.640
My dad's a big shot
in the Hero Association.

19:59.930 --> 20:00.890
Really?

20:00.970 --> 20:03.350
Yeah, I'm sure the Hero Association
won't sit back.

20:03.390 --> 20:05.140
They'll come and save me right away.

20:05.480 --> 20:08.440
Maybe I'll have them rescue you too,
while they're at it.

20:08.440 --> 20:11.020
- Really?
- I'll ask the heroes for you.

20:11.110 --> 20:12.520
Yes, please!

20:12.650 --> 20:16.530
- Then from now on, you work for me.
- Huh?

20:16.990 --> 20:17.990
You gotta problem?

20:18.200 --> 20:19.450
You wanna be rescued, right?

20:19.570 --> 20:20.570
Uh-huh.

20:20.820 --> 20:22.490
I wanna go home.

20:22.580 --> 20:24.540
What are you two talking about?

20:24.580 --> 20:26.290
Yikes! A monster!

20:26.620 --> 20:29.670
Sorry, but you two
are never going home.

20:29.750 --> 20:31.500
What a shame.

20:31.590 --> 20:34.050
If you don't let me
go home right now

20:34.090 --> 20:35.420
the heroes are gonna come!

20:36.970 --> 20:39.550
You're all gonna die.
The heroes and your dad too.

20:39.680 --> 20:43.560
All because they came to save you.
Everyone will die!

20:46.810 --> 20:48.600
Class-S heroes are coming, you know!

20:48.640 --> 20:51.610
You guys are going to
get your butts kicked!

20:51.690 --> 20:55.320
Yeah, Metal Bat alone
could take all of you out.

20:55.360 --> 20:58.070
I know. I saw him up close.
It'll be a piece of cake for him.

20:58.200 --> 21:01.370
Yeah, sure thing.
Ohh, I'm so scared of Metal Bat.

21:03.280 --> 21:07.700
Um...Waganma...
I saw on the news...

21:07.870 --> 21:10.960
All of 'em... Lightning Genji,
Heavy Kong, Metal Bat...

21:11.540 --> 21:13.710
And also Metal Knight...
just a while ago were...

21:14.090 --> 21:17.590
So? The Hero Association has
Tornado and Blast too.

21:17.800 --> 21:20.050
Oh yeah, and there's King too!

21:20.800 --> 21:21.640
How do you like that?

21:21.640 --> 21:23.470
I bet just hearing
that name scares you!

21:23.720 --> 21:28.310
Hey, kid. Do you even know why
the Monster Association was created?

21:28.480 --> 21:32.060
To wipe every last one
of those pests off the map.

21:32.350 --> 21:36.610
We knew from the start that
the Class-S heroes are insanely strong.

21:36.690 --> 21:38.400
But I'm still telling you.

21:38.440 --> 21:40.530
Every last hero will die.

21:41.070 --> 21:42.910
We've got crazy monsters
far more dangerous

21:42.910 --> 21:44.660
than the Class-S heroes.

21:44.910 --> 21:49.620
Especially our top monsters,
who are threat level Dragon.

21:56.880 --> 21:59.720
Possessing miraculous strength....

21:59.800 --> 22:04.010
They're like God's own works of art!

22:04.220 --> 22:06.850
Humans don't stand
a chance against them.

22:07.970 --> 22:09.600
Even King will die.

23:56.000 --> 24:00.890
COUNTERATTACK SIGNAL
